{
  "id": "m2_encapsulation_v1",
  "name": "Module 2: encapsulation (DEMO scale 30 x 20 mm, droplet generation NOT achievable)",
  "description": "DEMO SCALE: 75 x 25 mm drawn at 0.389 (uniform x/y, depths unchanged) into the 30 x 20 mm build area, then ports and routes repaired by hand; cad/generators/m2_encapsulation.py would regenerate the original, so do not rerun it over this file. *** THIS CHIP CANNOT MAKE CAPSULES AT THIS SCALE. *** The flow-focusing nozzle was 40 um wide; scaling gives 15.6 um; the 200 um open-channel floor clamps it to 200 um, 5x the original and 12.8x the scaled value (depth stays 40 um). Droplet generation at this size is not achievable by resin printing or hot embossing: a 40 um nozzle cannot be printed, and a 200 um nozzle will not give 70 um capsules. If the design drop ratio (70/40 = 1.75 x nozzle width) held, 200 um would give ~350 um capsules; 40 um depth confinement could pull it to ~130-200 um discs. Expect roughly 150-350 um, 2-5x the diameter, 10-100x the volume, untested. Options: (a) keep encapsulation OFF-CHIP on the existing commercial droplet kit and use this chip only for the finishing trap, cure and wash; (b) accept much larger capsules and re-check every downstream size limit. The pillar filters (30 and 100 um gaps) are also below the printable floor; the 25 um mesh is bought. PORTS 12 -> 6 (pitch >= 5 mm): emulsion_out + capsule_out -> m2_capsule_out_1 (off-chip selector valve; generator inlets closed during release); emulsion_in + breaker + buffer + photoinitiator -> m2_trap_in_1 (selector valve); oil_waste + waste + backflush -> m2_under_mesh_1 (selector valve). Capability lost: reagents can no longer be loaded simultaneously or kept on dedicated paths (carry-over and dead volume in the shared lines); oil and aqueous waste share a channel; no dedicated backflush path; the straight separation channel is 12.5 mm, not 15 mm; the cold delay stays off-chip as before. Ports are 0.8 mm.",
  "placeholder": true,
